ed by a $10 million PAC infusion", "Raters and prediction markets converge on a clear but not safe Democratic favorite"], "rationale": "Klobuchar combines strong name recognition, a dominant fundraising position, and a Democratic-leaning state, while raters (Likely D to Solid D) and markets pricing Democrats near 95% all point the same direction. Mid-September surveys show Demuth closing from fifteen points to the mid-single digits, which keeps this at Likely rather than Solid Democratic.", "watch": "The October 21 debate and heavy outside spending behind Demuth could extend her late polling momentum and narrow the margin further.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Tim Walz (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's governorship is open with Tim Walz retiring. Democrat Amy Klobuchar, a three-term senator with strong statewide name recognition, faces Republican Lisa Demuth. Klobuchar has raised roughly $7 million to Demuth's $360,000, though a Demuth-affiliated committee recently received a $10 million infusion, and outside spending has made this the most expensive governor's race in state history.\n\nPolls through mid-September show Klobuchar leading by anywhere from two to fifteen points, with the most recent surveys in the mid-to-high single digits. National ratings range from Likely D to Solid D, and prediction markets put Democratic chances around 93-95%. The race remains Likely Democratic, with the main open question being the size of the margin rather than the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 10.03}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9647, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.931, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9507, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9476, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9456, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9491, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9656, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-